[{:db/id -1, :doc/id "doc-ayatori-bench-coscientist-iteration-25", :doc/title "ayatori Co-Scientist Iteration 25 — full SF1 loads on the fleet host; the startup gate catches an IC09 defect on the first non-empty rung", :doc/path "bench/coscientist-iteration-25.edn", :doc/body "# Co-Scientist iteration 25 - full SF1 loads on the fleet host, and the startup gate earns its keep on the first non-empty rung\n\n> Seed: iteration 24's S2 - the footprint said full SF1 fits simeon.\n> Judge: bench/benchmark.edn v2; rung SF1 proper (all 1,003,605 posts,\n> every comment, every like); origin :cross-host, path :lan.\n\n## Generate\n\n  Prediction: ~20M quads, ~7 GB live, loads in minutes; the 11-op mix\n  runs with the empty share near zero; IC09 (now non-empty everywhere)\n  is the operation to watch.\n\n## Rank\n\n  First attempt: OutOfMemoryError at 13 GB inside transact-effective --\n  one transact over every quad holds every quad map and every effective\n  delta at once. Fix: build-kotobase makes a lazy quad seq and transacts\n  250,000 per batch; the db value accumulates.\n\n  Second attempt: 20,569,957 quads, load 13.8 s, build 92 s, RSS 9.1 GB,\n  used heap 11.6 of 11.8 GB max (garbage included; live ~6.9 GB at the\n  337 B/quad measured in iteration 24). It fits, with little room.\n\n  Then the 1,082-parameter startup gate, ~30 minutes on this rung (the\n  naive IC09 index twin materialises friend-of-friend messages over 3M\n  messages per parameter), returned:\n\n    checked 1082  disagreements 1  {:op :ic09 :person 17592186047707}\n\n  and disabled the index path. The gate did exactly what it is for.\n\n## Reflect - the defect\n\n  Iteration 18 put IC09's :limit 20 inside each half of the query and\n  excluded the start person AFTERWARDS (\"a friend's friend is you\").\n  When the start person's own messages sit in the two-hop top 20, the\n  exclusion leaves fewer than 20 rows and the rows the answer needed\n  were never fetched. Every official IC09 on the 35k subset was an\n  EMPTY answer, so the subset could not exercise it -- 98 parameters of\n  green that tested nothing about the limit. The first rung where IC09\n  answers caught it on the one parameter where it mattered.\n\n  Fix in two places: the exclusion moves INSIDE the query\n  (`[(not= ?x ?person)]`), so the limit is taken after it; and the\n  ordered drive (datalog f059e215) admits predicate clauses, running\n  each in the half its variables put it -- otherwise the exclusion\n  would have cost the drive. Tests: drive vs plain join with not= on\n  the two-hop shape, start person absent (127/290/0); kotobase-peer on\n  the new pin 262/804/0; the disagreeing parameter re-checked in-process\n  on full SF1: 20 rows both ways, sets equal.\n\n  Two lessons, both already in the workspace's rules and both paid again:\n  a gate whose inputs never reach the boundary (every answer empty) is a\n  gate that has passed once; and a rung is not just more of the same --\n  it is where the shapes the smaller rung never produced appear.\n\n## Meta\n\nVerdict: RUNG LOADED, GATE FOUND A DEFECT, no throughput row. The SUT was\nrestarted with the fix at 17:38; the gate takes ~30-40 minutes here, so\nthe SF1-proper row is iteration 26's. M3's first step (a rung above the\nsubset on the same host) is taken; SF3 would be ~60M quads and does not\nfit 16 GiB.\n\nSeeds for iteration 26, in order:\n\n  - S2' (the row): the 11-op mix on SF1 proper from levi, 8 and 32 slots;\n    empty share expected near 0; IC09 and IS3 the ones to watch; GC\n    pressure at a 13 GB ceiling is a named risk.\n  - S16 (gate cost): the IC09 index twin is the gate's 30 minutes;\n    rewrite it as the same ordered walk the Datalog path uses, or gate\n    IC09 on a sample of parameters with the full check as a separate\n    command.\n  - S17 (memory): 337 B/quad is four persistent index maps of boxed\n    strings; SF3 needs a third of that, and that is the persisted plane\n    (M3 proper).\n"}]
